# GitLab Software Delivery

## Description: <br>
Deliver a confirmed product requirement through architecture and documentation, implementation, build and test, independent review, GitLab merge-request and CI work, and final acceptance with directed feedback to the original development context. <br>

## Publisher: <br>
DevWerk <br>

## Category: <br>
software_delivery <br>

## Tags: <br>
- software-development <br>
- devops <br>
- gitlab <br>
- continuous-integration <br>
- requirement-baseline <br>
- code-review <br>

## Use Case: <br>
Use after the Conversation Agent has completed requirement discovery with the user and the product baseline, acceptance criteria, and GitLab repository are explicitly confirmed. <br>

## Selection Guide: <br>
Select only for a software delivery project with a frozen requirement baseline and GitLab delivery target. Continue requirement conversation instead when material questions remain open. <br>

## Loop Input: <br>
Product name and GitLab repository identity. Each Task Plan supplies its own confirmed requirement document. <br>

## Loop Output: <br>
Versioned design documents, implementation, build and test evidence, independent review, GitLab merge-request and CI evidence, and final acceptance. <br>

## Loop Version(s): <br>
1.0.0 <br>

